## Proof Pull
Existing HYP-3474 axes already reconstruct the private-firewall bit:
the count profile C, full colored-gate set F, numeric residues N, and
typed residues T are all pure for private_firewall_status.  However, no
subset of the existing axes preserves the full HYP-3490 route split.
The exact route sidecar R is the compact five-fiber route carrier, while
the incidence/projection sidecars I and Q are the compact three-fiber
private-status carriers.  The next proof-facing target is therefore a
finite incidence-cut lemma proving that the I/Q sidecars can be reduced
to dead-component/blocker-label multiplicity one without retaining row
names, plus a separate route reconstruction or route sidecar R.
